Raw: results/calibration/d2/d2_scaling.json

## profile-instrument finding (honest): cProfile is INAPPLICABLE to these C kernels.
Probed empirically: cProfile/lsprof records total_tt ~1.8e-05 s for 10 kernel calls
(~30ms real) even WITH cython -X profile=True, because lsprof only tracks Python-call
boundaries and the kernels make no Python subcalls. Replaced with a model-free overhead
decomposition: kernel_fraction = 1 - overhead/work, overhead measured at a near-zero-
compute config (csr passes=0 same arrays; pava n=64). Result: 99.99% both kernels.

